feat(cart): the cart domain joins — the first storefront write face, ownership stamped from the forwarded operator

Two services in one domain: CartService (the user's cart row — one
live row per user, a create idempotent against the existing one) and
CartItemService (the items — same-sku merge on repeat adds, quantity
bumps instead of duplicate rows). The golden DDL gains mall_carts
(unique per user_id) and mall_cart_items (cart cascade, indexed by
cart).

The item write face derives ownership from the forwarded x-user-id
metadata alone — the contract's CartItem carries no user field, so
the BFF's operator stamp IS the identity, and a bare call answers
BAD_REQUEST. The cart row materializes on demand (cart_for_user).

The app BFF's CoreTokenChecker now dials ValidateToken with its own
client type: the app face's tokens are minted into the ct=1 store,
and the checker was validating them against the ct=0 store — every
app-side gated call answered "access token expired". Each BFF pins
its own client in the session stage.

verified: app login (ct=1) mints an app store; add-to-cart answers
200 and the item lands (sku 1012, quantity 2); the repeat add merges
(quantity 4); the cart list reads back the full row
